        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NyGpDLxH4JyDuY5wbb7vbs",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022pages/concepts/flag-debt.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Flag Debt\\ndescription: Stale feature flags that persist after rollout completion, multiplying code paths and testing burden.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Feature-Flags\\n  - concept/Technical-Debt\\n  - pattern/Release-Management\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single authoritative source identifying the specific operational risk; no corroboration yet.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\nFlag debt accumulates when feature flags remain in the codebase after their rollout cycle completes. A flag removed promptly after successful rollout is invisible; one left behind becomes technical debt.\\n\\n## The Problem\\n\\nEach dormant flag represents a code path that must remain tested and maintained, even though it no longer serves a release purpose. As flags accumulate, they silently multiply the matrix of combinations the test suite must cover.\\n\\nThis is distinct from the operational benefit flags provide (decoupling deployment from release, enabling gradual user-facing rollout). Those operational wins are real and valuable. Flag debt is the cost of *not disciplining the cleanup*.\\n\\n## Cleanup Discipline\\n\\nSuccessful flag management requires:\\n\\n- **Flag lifecycle tracking**: Know when each flag was deployed and when rollout completed.\\n- **Removal deadline**: Set an explicit removal date shortly after rollout success (e.g., 1\\u20132 weeks).\\n- **Enforcement**: Make removal a blocking task in the release checklist, not an optional cleanup.\\n- **Audit**: Periodically scan the codebase for flags that have outlived their purpose.\\n\\nWithout active discipline, flags persist indefinitely because no one pays the cost of removal once the feature is live.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: eval://steering-adoption/sample-09 \\u2014 Feature flags and operational risk from flag debt accumulation.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
